            "Deposit and withdrawal accounting vulnerable to manipulated strategy valuations",
            "Yield claims and vault asset totals using externally reported prices",
            "Whether a depositor can dilute or extract value through stale, inflated, or deflated asset reports"
          ],
          "priority": 10,
          "reasoning": "WHY NOW: Vault is the primary accounting boundary for user shares, deposits, withdrawals, and yield, and its pricing depends on strategy-reported assets that may be manipulable through external market oracles, feeder rates, or Curve valuations. It is unvisited and has the highest concentration of critical price-dependent state. EXIT CRITERIA: Trace every path that computes share value or user payout through deposits, claims, withdrawals, and invested-asset updates; identify all upstream price sources and freshness/validation assumptions; determine whether a feasible manipulated price can mint excess shares, redeem disproportionate assets, or alter yield allocation; record concrete vulnerable flows or conclude no price-manipulation path exists.",
          "category": "aspect",
          "expected_impact": "medium"
        }
      ]
    },
