        {
          "goal": "Vulnerability analysis of SandclockFactory",
          "focus_areas": [
            "Whether factory-controlled deployments can initialize Vaults or strategies with attacker-controlled pricing sources, Curve pools, routers, token indices, or valuation parameters",
            "Whether CREATE2 deployment and caller-supplied initialization code permit deployment of incompatible or malicious pricing components that later influence share valuation",
            "Whether trust-gated deployment paths consistently restrict price-sensitive configuration and prevent unauthorized deployment or replacement of pricing logic"
          ],
          "priority": 7,
          "reasoning": "WHY NOW: SandclockFactory is an unvisited privileged deployment component, and its Vault/DCA deployment paths accept caller-supplied initialization code while creating contracts via CREATE2. Because Vault pricing depends on strategy-reported assets and external Curve/router data, a deployment-time configuration flaw could introduce a manipulable pricing source even if the already-reviewed Vault logic is correct. EXIT CRITERIA: Trace every factory deployment path and initialization parameter into price-sensitive contracts; verify authorization, code validation, immutable/configured pricing dependencies, and any ability for untrusted callers to select or alter pools, routers, token indices, or strategies. Conclude with either a concrete price-manipulation attack path and affected deployments or evidence that all such configuration is trust-gated and constrained.",
          "category": "aspect",
          "expected_impact": "high"
        }
      ]
    }
